<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-PROFILE OF PARIS-ROUBAIX WINNER.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-PROFILE OF PARIS-ROUBAIX WINNER.</headline>
<dateline>ROUBAIX 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Profile of Frenchman Frederic Guesdon, winner of the Paris-Roubaix classic on Sunday:</p>
<p>Age: 25</p>
<p>Height: 1.85 metres. Weight: 72 kgs.</p>
<p>Team: La Francaise des Jeux.</p>
<p>Professionnal debut: 1995.</p>
<p>Quick facts: Born in St Meen-le-Grand, the same village of Brittany as Louison Bobet, the 1956 Paris-Roubaix winner and three times Tour de France winner. Has changed team every year after joining Le Groupement in 1995 and Polti in 1996.</p>
<p>Leading victories: Haribo Classic 1997, Paris-Roubaix 1997.  </p>
<p>World Cup leading standings:</p>
<p>     1. Rolf Sorensen (Denmark)	 156 pts</p>
